        "collapsed": false,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 150,
        "body": "Water at 2 m/s through a 50 mm pipe, worked end to end. The **Reynolds number** says the flow is turbulent; the pipe's **roughness** (it reads the diameter in mm) and **Colebrook** give the friction factor; **Darcy–Weisbach** turns that into the pressure lost over 100 m of pipe. Change the velocity and watch every step follow.",
